WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.007
Think of a new phone. Two years later, the battery is weaker and the screen is scratched. Newer models have also come out, so it looks old-fashioned. It is worth much less than you paid.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:25.158
Business assets are the same. Depreciation is the fall in value of a non-current asset, such as machinery, motor vehicles or equipment, over its useful life.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:41.491
There are four causes. Wear and tear, from using the asset. Passage of time, as when a lease runs out. Obsolescence, when it goes out of date. And depletion, when a natural resource is used up.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:52.221
Count how many causes the question asks for. Pick that many from the four, and write each on its own numbered line, in a few words.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:01:08.595
Link each cause to an example. A van's tyres wear out: wear and tear. A ten-year lease runs out: passage of time. An old computer: obsolescence. A quarry being emptied: depletion.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:22.526
Here is a real question from June 2025. State two reasons why non-current assets depreciate. Two marks, so we need two different causes.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:31.637
Think of a machine in a factory. The more it is used, the more it wears out. That is cause one: wear and tear.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:41.718
Now think of a computer. Newer models make it out of date, even if it still works. That is cause two: obsolescence.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:51.761
Write each one on its own line. Passage of time or depletion would also be correct. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:02:03.736
A common mistake is giving the purpose of depreciation, spreading the cost, instead of a cause. The question asks why the value falls.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:13.772
Another is writing the same cause twice in different words. Usage and wear and tear are one idea, so they earn only one mark.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:27.523
Now you try. Read about the taxi company, and give three different causes of depreciation, each with an example from the business. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:42.842
Wear and tear: the cars wear out because they are driven every day. Obsolescence: the booking system goes out of date when newer software appears. Passage of time: the five-year lease runs out.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:53.847
Remember: four causes, wear and tear, passage of time, obsolescence and depletion. Give different ideas, one per line. Now try the practice questions.
